Well, I finally got PL5 to work on THINKC4, with the STRONGHOLD
option.  The only bug I found in Makedefs was that it writes the
monster resource to makedefs.rsrc, and not Nethack.rsrc.  You can use
ResEdit to cut and paste between the two.  Also remember to re-comment
the #define MAKEDEFS_C 1 statements in macfile.c and monst.c when
compiling the main application.

If anyone wants the compiled version, send me e-mail.  If you want a
list of the changes I made to get STRONGHOLD to work (and any other
bugs), also send me e-mail.  I'm on travel until next Friday (Nov 3),
but will reply as soon as I get back

Thanks to everyone who sent me fixes for bugs.


